cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dcGO Pipeline, please cite this software and the method references in the README."
title: "dcGO Pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bolser"
    given-names: "Dan"
    email: "dan.bolser@outsee.co.uk"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dbolser/dcGO-2.0"
url: "https://github.com/dbolser/dcGO-2.0"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A reimplementation of the domain-centric Gene Ontology (dcGO) method that
  statistically associates InterPro protein domains and supra-domains with
  ontology terms, using Fisher's exact tests with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR
  control and optional True Path Rule propagation. Besides the Gene Ontology it
  can associate domains with any of the other registered vocabularies (Enzyme
  Commission, Reactome, UniProt keywords, subcellular locations, ChEBI ligands
  and cofactors, and further UniProt-native cross-references).
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - protein function prediction
  - protein domains
  - Gene Ontology
  - InterPro
  - UniProt
  - Enzyme Commission
references:
  - type: article
    title: "dcGO: database of domain-centric ontologies on functions, phenotypes, diseases and more"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Fang"
        given-names: "Hai"
      - family-names: "Gough"
        given-names: "Julian"
    journal: "Nucleic Acids Research"
    volume: 41
    issue: "D1"
    start: "D536"
    end: "D544"
    year: 2013
    doi: "10.1093/nar/gks1080"
    notes: "The method this pipeline reimplements."
